# Line endings: text files are kept with LF (Unix) line endings in the repository and in your checkout, on every
# system. Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks files out with CRLF and warns
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for every file an editor or tool saves with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF to run reliably.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.stl binary
*.step binary
*.stp binary
*.brep binary
*.pdf binary
